  "narrative": "The newly delivered validation evidence resolves one candidate lead and leaves the remaining feature_063 signal scientifically ambiguous rather than clinically established. For H89 (outcome_008, feature_008 1 vs 0, claimed stronger dependency), discovery R73 was nominally supportive: signed estimate +0.0322, interval [0.0028, 0.0617]. However, its lower bound was well below the outcome_008 clinical benchmark (about 0.028), and independent validation R90 was not supportive: signed estimate -0.0033, interval [-0.0500, 0.0434]. The validation point estimate is negligible, the sign is opposite to the claimed direction, and the interval includes no effect, clinically meaningful effects in either direction, and imprecision that cannot support a clinically significant difference. Therefore H89 is rejected and closed. This is another non-replication of a discovery-only marginal association in the feature_008/feature_047-related high-prevalence binary family.\n\nFor H148 (outcome_014, feature_063 level_002 vs level_001, direction +1, meaning a raw higher, less-negative dependency score in exposed relative to comparator), the evidence is more nuanced. Discovery R101 gave signed estimate +0.0361, interval [0.0022, 0.0701], so the point estimate is clinically sizable relative to the outcome_014 absolute-mean benchmark of roughly 0.0093, but the lower bound allows clinically subthreshold effects and only barely excludes zero. Independent validation R117 is same-sign but imprecise: signed estimate +0.0234, interval [-0.0271, 0.0740]. The point estimate again exceeds the approximate 10% benchmark, but the validation interval includes zero and clinically subthreshold values, and these independent intervals are conservative because they account for the validation budget and the large number of validation comparisons in the run. Taken together, the two estimates favor the proposed direction, but they do not establish a scientifically meaningful difference with adequate precision. Therefore I do not accept H148; I keep it unresolved. It remains the best remaining dataset-specific uncertainty because it is the only feature_063 contrast with discovery evidence excluding zero, and the independent validation was not opposed, but its uncertainty is too large to license an accepted claim.\n\nThe surrounding feature_063 evidence does not strengthen the claim enough to change that judgment. H149 (outcome_006, same contrast, signed positive direction) is directionally consistent but not decisive: discovery R102 is +0.0218, interval [-0.0126, 0.0563], with both lower and upper bounds permitting no effect or subthreshold effects. The level_003 versus level_001 and level_003 versus level_002 checks for outcome_014/outcome_006 have positive point estimates but very wide intervals because level_003 has only 98 observations, so they cannot establish dose-response. The stratum checks within feature_008=1 remain positive but are also not decisive. Cross-outcome checks for outcome_008 and outcome_011 do not support extension beyond the near-zero outcome_014/outcome_006 pair. Thus the feature_063 family remains dataset-specific and unaccepted.\n\nThe broader scientific conclusion for the current evidence base is unchanged: no association has yet met the combined threshold of clinically meaningful effect size, sufficient precision, multiplicity control, and independent validation. The new H89 validation adds a negative finding. H148 remains the principal unresolved lead, but it should not be described as a supported predictor-subgroup association. All conclusions remain associations within the supplied dataset and do not establish causality or generalizability.\n\nThe most informative next analysis is to test whether the H148 signal is coherent in the paired near-zero outcome outcome_006 and in a prespecified clinical-feature subgroup. I registered mean-difference refinements for outcome_014 and outcome_006, feature_063 level_002 versus level_001 within feature_024 >= -7.353, the observed median split of this numeric clinical feature, plus an interaction refinement for outcome_014. If feature_063 shows a coherent clinically meaningful pattern in these targeted subgroup comparisons or if H149 gains clinically decisive evidence, H148 and H149 could be revisited together. If these focused subgroup analyses remain imprecise or attenuate the effect, the feature_063 family should be closed without further validation.",
