ture_042/feature_034 pattern is heterogeneous rather than a single coherent dependency-program effect. The outcome_014 signal remains strongest in feature_034=1, and H221 and H220 suggest that the complement effect is imprecise rather than clean, but not decisive enough to claim interaction specificity. Outcome_006 has suggestive same-direction extension evidence in H227 and the symmetric main-effect candidate H223, but the intervals are wide and cross zero. The most important unresolved opposite-sign candidate is outcome_008: full-population H208, localized H217, and feature_045=0-restricted H228 all favor a less negative outcome_008 score for feature_042=1, i.e. weaker dependency, and several intervals exclude zero, but their lower bounds are below the approximate absolute-mean 10% benchmark for outcome_008 (about 0.0282). Thus this is an active unresolved lead, not an accepted finding.\\n\\nOther major negative or closed families reduce optimism about broad predictor effects: the feature_023 lead failed validation for outcome_007 and was not robust in outcome_001 subgroup contexts; many feature_009, feature_048, feature_063, feature_054, and binary-feature contrasts were null, opposite, underpowered, or clinically imprecise. These are negative findings in this supplied dataset; they do not establish true absence in a broader population.\\n\\nNo new validation is possible because the validation budget is exhausted. The most informative next analyses are the already registered internal localization tests H230-H233. H230 is the priority test for the outcome_008 opposite-direction candidate, asking whether the feature_042 weaker-dependency signal is localized within feature_045=0 and specifically to feature_034=1. H231-H233 test the symmetric feature_034 main-effect pattern among feature_042=1 and feature_045=0 samples for outcome_014, outcome_006, and outcome_008. For outcome_014 and outcome_006 negative-direction claims, signed positive support means stronger dependency in the exposed condition; for outcome_008 positive-direction claims, signed positive support means weaker dependency. I would consider acceptance only if the interval lower bound clears the relevant approximate absolute-mean 10% benchmark and the direction is coherent with the local evidence; otherwise these remain unresolved associations in this dataset only.",
