  "narrative": "No new independent validation was delivered and no response deadlines are due. The voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so this synthesis treats all remaining conclusions as supplied-dataset associations rather than causal effects or generalizable biomarkers. I close the only active untested refinement, H268, because an additional post hoc interaction test in the same data would not address the decisive limitations of this final state: multiplicity, lack of independent replication, and possible confounding by the unadjusted observational structure.\n\nSupported findings. The only evidence that I regard as scientifically meaningful after considering magnitude, precision, and prior multiplicity is a narrow outcome_014 association in a localized feature context. Outcome estimates are already signed to the hypothesis direction, so positive signed values mean the exposed group has a more negative CRISPR dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency. For outcome_014, a working 10%-scale benchmark is roughly 0.0093 because the absolute mean is about 0.093. H203/R170 is the broad envelope within feature_034=1: feature_042=1 versus feature_042=0 has signed estimate +0.058, interval +0.009 to +0.107. This is accepted but should not be read as a general feature_042 effect because the lower bound is at the benchmark and the pattern becomes much stronger in higher feature_024 strata. The clearest accepted contrast is H238/R205: within feature_034=1 and feature_024 at or above median, feature_042=1 versus feature_042=0 has signed estimate +0.104, interval +0.038 to +0.169. The lower bound far exceeds the outcome_014 benchmark, so this supports a clinically meaningful, stronger-dependency association in this dataset. H249/R216 refines the same feature_042 contrast to feature_034=1, feature_024 at or above median, and feature_045=0: +0.094, interval +0.019 to +0.169. H252/R219 gives the symmetric feature_034 contrast within feature_042=1 and feature_024 at or above median: +0.099, interval +0.016 to +0.183. H260/R232 narrows the feature_042 contrast to the upper feature_024 quartile within feature_034=1: +0.156, interval +0.062 to +0.249. These claims are not independent validations; they are nested and overlapping tests in the same 2000-observation dataset, but together they are consistent with a localized stronger-dependency pattern when feature_034 and feature_042 are both positive and feature_024 is high.\n\nNegative or non-supported findings. The high feature_024 pattern is context-specific: H250/R217 tests feature_034=1 versus feature_034=0 within feature_042=0 and feature_024 at or above median and is near null: +0.002 interval -0.076 to +0.072. This supports specificity but is not proof of absence. H262/R234 tests the feature_042 contrast in the lower feature_024 quartile within feature_034=1: +0.008, interval -0.092 to +0.109, with no support for a clinically meaningful difference. H239/R206 in a lower feature_024 context is imprecise and unresolved, not evidence of absence. Several broader predictor claims were either null, underpowered, inconsistent, or failed independent validation. H1/R1 and validation R77 do not support a feature_002 outcome_001 association. H89 discovery suggested outcome_008 but validation R90 failed. H76/R151 suggested outcome_007 with feature_023, but validation R166 was null. H145 and validation R103 failed for outcome_006 feature_052. H146/R101 was rejected, and the reverse H148 plus validation R117 remains unresolved but not supported. H171 and especially H182/R143 versus validation R155 showed a promising feature_023 outcome_001 subgroup effect that did not replicate. H202/R169 discovery for outcome_001 feature_042 failed independent validation R179. These validation failures argue strongly against treating any broad or non-narrow predictor contrast as a reliable finding.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty. The strongest unresolved signal is outcome_008. There are multiple interval-excluding-zero contrasts suggesting weaker dependency with feature_042=1 in feature_034 and high feature_024 contexts: H208/R174 +0.030 interval +0.005 to +0.054; H217/R188 +0.041 interval +0.008 to +0.075; H228/R199 +0.041 interval +0.002 to +0.079; H240/R207 +0.057 interval +0.007 to +0.108; H256/R228 +0.042 interval +0.006 to +0.078. However the working outcome_008 benchmark is about 0.0282, and these lower bounds are below it. Therefore the pattern is suggestive but not sufficient to claim a clinically meaningful association, especially after iterative subgroup selection. The direct upper-quartile specificity test for outcome_014, H261/R233, has a large point estimate but an interval lower bound near the benchmark and wide imprecision, so it remains unresolved. H253/R225, H254/R226, H255/R227, and other interaction leads do not robustly clear their benchmarks after multiplicity caution. H234/R220 is interval-supported for outcome_014 within feature_034=1 and feature_063=level_002, but I keep it unresolved because it is a post hoc feature_063 localization and no independent validation remains. Correlated outcome_006 extensions, including H265/R237, are too imprecise.\n\nNext investigation. The most informative next analysis is not further mining of this dataset. If an external or pre-specified holdout cohort becomes available, test exactly the accepted outcome_014 contexts: feature_034=1 with feature_042=1 and feature_024 at or above median, the upper feature_024 quartile, and the feature_045=0 subset. Treat the finding as replicable only if the independent interval lower bound remains above the outcome_014 clinical benchmark of about 0.0093. Separately, outcome_008 should be reopened only if the exact feature_042 weaker-dependency contexts achieve an independent lower bound above about 0.0282. Any future supplied-dataset analysis should use pre-specified multiplicity control and, if possible, covariate adjustment; unadjusted Welch contrasts are adequate for descriptive associations here but not for causal inference.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 20 final synthesis. Validation budget exhausted. Only supported final findings are supplied-dataset associations for outcome_014: H203/R170 broad envelope within feature_034=1, +0.058 [0.009,0.107]; H238/R205 strongest within feature_034=1 and feature_024 at or above median, +0.104 [0.038,0.169]; H249/R216 same contrast within feature_045=0, +0.094 [0.019,0.169]; H252/R219 symmetric feature_034 contrast within feature_042=1 and feature_024 at or above median, +0.099 [0.016,0.183]; H260/R232 upper feature_024 quartile within feature_034=1, +0.156 [0.062,0.249]. Interpret positive signed outcome_014 estimates as stronger dependency, not causality or generalizability. Negative/context specificity: H250/R217 near null when feature_042=0; H262/R234 no lower-quartile support. Failed or unresolved broad claims include H1, H76, H89, H145, H146/H148, H171/H182, H202. Outcome_008 feature_042 pattern remains unresolved: H208, H217, H228, H240, H256 exclude zero but lower bounds below benchmark ~0.0282. H234 clears benchmark but post hoc feature_063 localization remains unresolved. Closed H268 as untested post hoc interaction because no independent validation can resolve remaining uncertainty. Next useful step is exact external replication with pre-specified multiplicity control, accepting outcome_014 only if lower bound remains above ~0.0093 and outcome_008 only if lower bound remains above ~0.0282."
